    <!-- About & help -->
    <string name="version">Version</string>
    <string name="help_no_lights">The lights don\'t turn on</string>
    <string name="help_no_sound">Music mode doesn\'t react</string>
    <string name="help_buttons">The colour buttons do nothing</string>
    <string name="help_stutter">The video stutters</string>
    <string name="licences">Licences</string>
    <string name="reset_all">Reset everything</string>
    <string name="reset_all_hint">Every setting back to its default. The lights restart.</string>
    <string name="help_no_lights_text">1. Check the controller is plugged in: Home shows the USB state while the lights are on.\n2. The first time, Android asks to allow the app to use the controller: press OK.\n3. Check the baud rate matches the controller\'s firmware (LED strip › Controller).\n4. Press Red to turn the lights on, or use Home.</string>
    <string name="help_no_sound_text">Music mode listens to what the TV plays. It can\'t hear Live TV\'s tuner or sound sent as Dolby to a soundbar.\n\nIn Music mode › Audio source, try Output mix, then Playback capture (Android 13 and later), and use Test audio input.</string>
    <string name="help_buttons_text">The colour buttons need Remote shortcuts on (Settings › Remote buttons). With USB debugging allowed, the app turns it on itself; otherwise turn on \"TV Ambient remote buttons\" in Android\'s Accessibility settings.\n\nIn Live TV the buttons pass through to teletext unless you change \"Not in Live TV\".</string>
    <string name="help_stutter_text">Capturing the screen costs the TV some work. Lower Screen mode › Captures per second, or use Shell screenshots instead of Screen recording.\n\n4K at 60 frames a second is the hardest case on this kind of TV.</string>
    <string name="licences_text">TV Ambient: MIT licence.\n\nusb-serial-for-android (mik3y): MIT licence.\n\nInter typeface (Rasmus Andersson and contributors): SIL Open Font License 1.1.\n\nThe icon\'s letters are our own dot-matrix drawing.\n\nTV Ambient does not copy screens, text, icons or colours from other ambient-light apps.</string>

